Yi-Teng Huang is an Assistant Professor in the Graduate Institute of Photonics and
Optoelectronics and the Department of Electrical Engineering at National Taiwan University,
where he founded the Novel Inorganic Materials Lab in August 2025.

He studied Physics at National Tsing Hua University (B.S., 2013) and Applied Physics at
National Taiwan University (M.S., 2015, with Prof. Ding Ping Tsai), then completed his PhD in
Physics at the University of Cambridge in 2023 under Prof. Akshay Rao and Prof. Robert Hoye.
Before returning to Taiwan he was a postdoctoral researcher in the Department of Inorganic
Chemistry at the University of Oxford.

His work uses ultrafast spectroscopy to understand how charge carriers behave in
perovskite-inspired semiconductors, and turns that understanding into better photovoltaic and
optoelectronic devices.
